-- title:
--   Differentials of an affine dilatation along a coordinate centre
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a discrete valuation ring (a commutative domain with the `IsDiscreteValuationRing` property) and let $\pi \in R$ be an element whose span is the maximal ideal of $R$. Let $C$ be a commutative $R$-algebra which is smooth over $R$, let $r, n$ be natural numbers, and let $y : \mathrm{Fin}\,r \to C$ and $z : \mathrm{Fin}\,n \to C$ be families of elements of $C$. Assume given a basis $b$ of the $C$-module $\Omega_{C/R}$ indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,r \sqcup \mathrm{Fin}\,n$ whose left-hand members are the universal derivations $b(\mathrm{inl}\,i) = d y_i$ and whose right-hand members are $b(\mathrm{inr}\,j) = d z_j$. Write $J \subseteq C$ for the ideal generated by the image $\pi_C$ of $\pi$ in $C$ together with all the $z_j$, and let $C'$ be the affine dilatation [`AffineDilatation.Ring`](def/RingTheory_AffineDilatation.html#L20) $J\,\pi_C$, that is, by definition the $C$-subalgebra $\mathrm{adjoin}_C(\mathtt{gen}\;J\;\pi_C)$ of the localisation of $C$ away from $\pi_C$. The assertion is that there exists a basis $b'$ of the $C'$-module $\Omega_{C'/R}$, indexed by the same set $\mathrm{Fin}\,r \sqcup \mathrm{Fin}\,n$, such that $b'(\mathrm{inl}\,i)$ is the universal derivation of the image of $y_i$ in $C'$ for every $i$, and such that $\pi \cdot b'(\mathrm{inr}\,j)$, the image of $\pi$ in $C'$ acting on $b'(\mathrm{inr}\,j)$, equals the universal derivation of the image of $z_j$ in $C'$ for every $j$.
--
--   This is the statement that dilating a smooth $R$-algebra along a centre $(\pi, z_1,\dots,z_n)$ cut out by part of a system of coordinates again yields a free module of differentials, on $dy_i$ and on elements $dz_j'$ with $dz_j = \pi\,dz_j'$, as in the theory of dilatations and Néron models of Bosch–Lütkebohmert–Raynaud. It is used in the Néron model infrastructure to bound the smoothness defect of an affine dilatation, via the resulting inclusion of lattices of differentials with index $n$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AffineDilatation_exists_basis_kaehlerDifferential_of_smooth_of_basis.lean

import Mathlib
